## WAYLAND_DISPLAY doesn't exist until Hyprland starts, so importing it (and
## HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE, needed by anything using Hyprland's IPC —
## waybar's hyprland module, hypridle's hyprctl dispatch calls — neither of
## which would otherwise work once started by systemd --user, a separate
## process tree that never automatically inherits vars Hyprland sets on
## itself after its own exec) into the systemd/D-Bus activation
## environment — and starting the graphical session target that owns
## Waybar/Mako/hypridle/swaybg — happens here rather than in hypr-session.

exec-once = systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE && systemctl --user start dotfiles-graphical-session.target
